comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T10:27:25.583Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: health --check-only now defaults to summary verdict output with empty passing evidence bodies; --full retains complete diagnostics and explicit brief/summary preserve fast optional-scan behavior."
  "2026-07-30T11:24:16.147Z","harness:codex","Delivery boundary: --check-only now returns the summary verdict by default while still running every check, and --full restores evidence. The canonical issue remains open until health is added to the representative token-budget corpus with measured before/after evidence and agent-guidance coverage."
  "2026-07-30T11:30:57.231Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/829 reviews cohesive SDK context budgets, universal row contracts, bounded graph/health diagnostics, quality ratchets, and exact-head commit e53544cd1."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T09:21:19.724Z","harness:claude-code","Re-measured 2026-07-30 at HEAD, after PR 818 shipped bounded projections and snapshot lease safety. The bounded-projection wave did not reach this command. pm health plain = 127,582 B; pm health --check-only = 127,583 B (one byte MORE than plain); pm health --summary = 727 B. The cheap form is 175x smaller than the form AGENTS.md routes agents to under When Unsure, and --check-only remains exactly as inert as when this item was filed. A new bounded-projection primitive existing in the SDK while this consumer cannot reach it is the seam pattern, not a fix."
